---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Scientific Library"
  description="The PeptiBloom Scientific Library is a public research resource built to make evidence, uncertainty, provenance and unanswered questions inspectable."
>
  <section class="page-hero section">
    <div class="site-frame page-hero__grid page-hero__grid--library">
      <div class="page-hero__copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Scientific Library</p>
        <h1>Research should be easier to inspect than marketing.</h1>
        <p class="page-hero__lead">
          This library is being built around evidence, transparency and traceability. Scientific entries will
          appear only after they complete the approved review path; the web will not invent content to make the
          library look fuller than it is.
        </p>
        <div class="hero__actions" aria-label="Library actions">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="#publication-state">See the publication standard</a>
          <a class="editorial-link" href="/methodology/">Read the methodology <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="library-cover" aria-labelledby="library-cover-title">
        <div class="library-cover__topline">
          <span>PeptiBloom Scientific Library</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        </div>
        <div class="library-cover__halo" aria-hidden="true">
          <span></span><span></span><span></span>
        </div>
        <p class="surface-kicker">Reading standard</p>
        <h2 id="library-cover-title">What is known. What is not. Where it comes from.</h2>
        <div class="library-cover__footer">
          <span>Evidence</span><span>Uncertainty</span><span>Provenance</span>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--quiet" aria-labelledby="library-principles-title">
    <div class="site-frame">
      <div class="section-heading reading-column">
        <p class="eyebrow">Library principles</p>
        <h2 id="library-principles-title">What a PeptiBloom scientific entry is expected to make visible.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="library-principles library-principles--cards">
        <article class="library-principle">
          <span><small>01</small>Evidence</span>
          <p>What the available research can support — without extending beyond it.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="library-principle">
          <span><small>02</small>Uncertainty</span>
          <p>What remains theoretical, disputed, incomplete or unknown.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="library-principle">
          <span><small>03</small>Provenance</span>
          <p>Where information comes from and how a reader can trace it back.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="library-principle">
          <span><small>04</small>Contradictions</span>
          <p>Where sources or findings do not align cleanly.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="publication-state" aria-labelledby="current-library-title">
    <div class="site-frame feature-layout feature-layout--publication">
      <div class="feature-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Current publication state</p>
        <h2 id="current-library-title">No placeholder compounds. No fabricated evidence.</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">
          PeptiBloom will publish compound-level scientific pages only when an approved Evidence contract and
          production-ready scientific content are available. Until then, this page explains the publication
          standard rather than pretending finished entries already exist.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="publication-ledger" aria-labelledby="why-this-matters-title">
        <div class="publication-ledger__heading">
          <p class="surface-kicker">Why this matters</p>
          <span>Review gate</span>
        </div>
        <h3 id="why-this-matters-title">A gap is better than invented certainty.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><span>Scientific Inventory</span><strong>Source and review workflow</strong></li>
          <li><span>Evidence</span><strong>Public contract required</strong></li>
          <li><span>Library entry</span><strong>Published only when ready</strong></li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Missing content is visible by design. The library does not use mock studies, unsupported claims or
          unreviewed copy as a substitute for production-ready scientific material.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft" aria-labelledby="next-title">
    <div class="site-frame method-callout">
      <div class="method-callout__marker" aria-hidden="true"><span>01</span><span>04</span></div>
      <div class="reading-column">
        <p class="eyebrow">How to read PeptiBloom</p>
        <h2 id="next-title">Start with the method, then follow the sources.</h2>
        <p>
          The methodology explains how PeptiBloom approaches provenance, interpretation, contradictions and the
          boundary between scientific information and commercial information.
        </p>
        <a class="button button--primary" href="/methodology/">Read the methodology</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="research-tools-title">
    <div class="site-frame feature-layout research-tools-band">
      <div class="feature-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Research tools</p>
        <h2 id="research-tools-title">Useful now, without pretending the scientific catalogue is finished.</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">
          The concentration and reconstitution calculator is available as a transparent arithmetic tool. Its
          formulas, limits and worked example are visible on the page.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="research-tools-band__action">
        <p class="surface-kicker">Transparent arithmetic</p>
        <div class="research-tools-band__units" aria-hidden="true"><span>mg/mL</span><span>µg/mL</span><span>mL</span></div>
        <a class="button button--primary" href="/calculator/">Use the calculator</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
